          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
            %p
              We observe that the given formula in fact establishes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              between the two kinds of actions:
            %p
              First, notice by the decomposition
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ElementInSemidirectProductAsProductOfElementsInSubgroups"} (7)
              in Remark
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomomOutOfSemidirectProductGroupFixedByItsRestrictionToSubgroups"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋊
                      %mi α
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G} \rtimes_\alpha G
              can be written in the form
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ActionOfSemidirectProductFromEquivariantComponentActions"} (9)
              for some actions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a{:href => "action#eq:ActionPropertyOfGroupActions"} action property
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                  is equivalently the action property of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,\rho)
                  on elements of the form
                  = succeed ";" do
