            %p
              In conclusion,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,\rho)
              is an action of the semidirect product group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %msub
                      %mo ⋊
                      %mi α
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G} \rtimes_\alpha G
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a
              = succeed "-equivariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              This implies immediately that the condition for a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X
              to be an action homomorphisms on both sides are the same.
            %p
              And so the functor
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:EquivalenceBetweenEquivariantActionsAndSemidirecProductActions"} (8)
              is in fact an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              on both objects as well as morphisms, hence in particular is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+bundle"} equivariant bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariance+group"}> equivariance group
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
          %p
            %br/
